Histamine poisoning can cause a rash called urticaria. Urticaria is an allergic reaction that causes red, raised bumps to appear on your skin. These bumps are also known as hives. They're often itchy and may sting or burn.

The histamine in your immune system triggers the release of fluid into the small blood vessels just under your skin. This fluid leaks out into the tissues beneath your skin, causing swelling. As a result, tiny blood vessels leak fluid into the spaces between cells in your skin, resulting in redness and raised welts.

